790:
(a) Filing generally. A person seeking issuance of an event permit shall file an application with the city administrator or his designee on forms provided by such officer.
(b) Filing period. An application for an event permit shall be filed with the city administrator or his designee not less than five business days nor more than 60 calendar days before the date on which it is proposed to conduct the event.
(c) Late applications. The city administrator or his designee, where good cause is shown therefor, shall have the authority to consider any application under this division which is filed less than five business days before the date such event is proposed to be conducted.
(d) Contents. The application for an event permit shall set forth the following information:
(1) The name, address and telephone number of the person seeking to conduct such event;
(2) If the event is proposed to be conducted for, by or on behalf of an organization, the name, address and telephone number of the headquarters of the organization, and the authorized and responsible heads of such organization;
(3) The name, address and telephone number of the person who will be the event chairperson and who will be responsible for its conduct;
(4) The date when the event is to be conducted;
(5) The location of the event;
(6) The approximate number of persons and their ages, to constitute such event;
(7) The hours when such event is to start and terminate;
(8) The location by streets of any assembly areas for the event, and streets and/or intersections where the event is to be held;
(9) The time at which units of the event will begin to assemble at any such assembly area and/or street;
(10) If the event is designed to be held by or on behalf of any person other than the applicant, a communication in writing from the person proposing to hold the event, authorizing the applicant to apply for the permit on his behalf;
(11) Any additional information that the city administrator or his designee shall find reasonably necessary for a fair determination as to whether the proposed event will endanger public health, safety or welfare.
(e) Application fee. Applicants shall pay an event fee per event. The fee shall be in an amount as established by the mayor and council from time to time.
(f) Release. Applicants shall provide a release from each participant in the event regarding solicitation of contributions from traffic on city streets.
(Ord. No. 09-09-24, § 97.009, 9-24-2009)

